      "summary": "The candidate splits NSC-066 revision 7 into three concrete single-agent children: (1) title-screen-start-game-transition owning TitleScreenController.cs and TitleScreenPlayModeTests.cs for title visibility, the PlayerMovement and PlayerInteractionController suspension, and the one-shot Start Game transition; (2) title-screen-chase-backdrop owning the new TitleScreenChaseBackdrop MonoBehaviour and its Play Mode fixture, driven in memory through a public Tick(float) seam with an injected seed, interval selector and side selector; (3) title-screen-transparent-layout-build owning DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.cs, TitleScreenSceneBuilderTests.cs and Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, which removes the opaque fill, restacks the three sayings and the chunky Start Game Button to the left while preserving the pinned hierarchy, computes the floor segment, adds and configures exactly one backdrop component, and materializes the scene. Parent identity is copied exactly at revision 7 with contract sha f6c2bdb4. The 10 parent exclusive resources partition 3/4/3 with TitleScreenController.cs and the builder plus scene on separate children. All 14 parent entries carry exactly one coverage record and all 18 child entries are traced. The headline improvement this round is correct: parent revision 7 folded the TitleCard hierarchy constraint into AC-001, and the candidate splits that into child 3 AC-001 for the transparent Image and left-stacked layout and child 3 AC-002 for preserving TitleScreen to TitleCard to StartGameButton, stripping rather than deleting TitleCard and keeping its RectTransform left-anchored so the anchorMax.x caps measure against the right container, naming the four fixtures and five line numbers. Repository verification at head 12c6d824 confirmed every premise: the five call sites resolve that exact path at WizardSelectionPlayModeTests.cs lines 44 and 91, WizardGameEntryPlayModeTests.cs line 310, WizardAnimationPlayModeTests.cs line 548 and 